fork() – Creates a child process.
exec() – Executes the given Linux command.
wait() – Makes the parent process wait for the child process.
getpid() – Returns the Process ID.
getppid() – Returns the Parent Process ID.

Linux Commands Used
uname -a -Displays information about the Linux OS and kernel.
lscpu - Displays CPU information.
lsblk - Displays storage and block-device information.
ps - Displays currently running processes.
top - Displays real-time system activity.
OS and Hardware Abstraction

The Operating System acts as a bridge between hardware and application programs. It manages hardware resources and provides services to applications.
CPU: The OS uses processes and scheduling. The scheduler decides which process gets CPU time.
Memory: The OS provides each process with its own virtual address space.
Storage: The OS provides files, directories, and file systems instead of requiring programs to directly access disk sectors.
I/O Devices: The OS uses device drivers to communicate with devices such as keyboards, displays, and disks. Applications use system calls to access them.
